    "turn_idx": 5,
    "turn_text": "Well, as you know, Ralph, Social Security, and now the last time Congress did anything major with it was 38 years ago. And 38 years ago, they compromised and they rightfully should and had a bipartisan bill, but it had many weaknesses. And so Social Security has not been expanded the way that it needs to be. It is the lifeline for the American people. It's our number one insurance program. Both you and I have spent a lot of time talking to the people and reminding them, as Republicans try to say that Social Security is an",
