    "turn_idx": 16,
    "turn_text": "Well, we're talking about going back and looking at the whole tax reform act that the Republicans acted in 2017. and having a whole-scale change of that, and including as part of that, you know, looking at the IRS, you're absolutely right in terms of how they've been defunded. And what we need to do is make sure that we're funding them at a level, and especially so that all corporations, there should be a bare minimum that you have to pay. I don't care how many lawyers and the accountants you can hire, you belong to a country that serves and protects and provides the kind of climate for you to prosper and and grow, and you know, Ralph, better than anyone else, the disparity that exists today is just proud to say that a lot of people, even a friend, I know you know Bob Patricelli as well, but a former CEO of Cigna who said, listen, we've got to change this. Let's take the idea and concept of entrepreneurialism and capitalism and make sure that everybody participates it. And we're going to be introducing legislation on that that will require, if you're going to be able to get a capital gains and dividends break, You got to make sure that you're also providing your employees with those stock options where they can grow their own personal wealth and shift a lot of this that's going on. But there's going to be massive change in terms of both tackling the tax code issues and changing that the revenues there again. And that'll be a major fight. We have control of both the House and the Senate, but it's very slim margins that will control both. Obviously, the vice president breaking a tie in the Senate. And we have, as of today, 222 members in the House. And as you know, it takes 218 to pass a bill.",
