    "turn_idx": 21,
    "turn_text": "I think that first and foremost, we've probably heard it in Nancy Pelosi's remarks the other night. And certainly that is going to be the focus of the Ways and Means Committee as much as we have a lot of important issues. And you can do a lot of this simultaneously as well. But the initial thrust and emphasis is going to be on directly tackling this pandemic, making sure that we're getting the relief out to the states that they need coordinating in such a manner. I mean, I don't know why we haven't gone to the Defense Production Act and utilizing the Defense Logistic Agency, especially as it relates to vaccines and getting those vaccines out there as well. And then also getting money back into the hands of people. Now, I would argue that another way to do that is through Social Security, but no matter how you shape or scope it, we've got to get money back into the hands of people. We also put the country back to work by way of massive infrastructure, which we've talked about. The House has passed, but now we have the ability to do that. And then all of that, as you point out, is going to have to have us turn back to the revenue side and look at the fairness of that. I mean, we've got Obama proposed back as well, and we ought to go back and take a look at You know, what Obama was proposing and including incentives in there for manufacturers, especially of goods made here in our country, where we're going to be putting Americans back to work, et cetera, but also stepping up on the infrastructure requirements,",
