  {
    "episode_id": 87450,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/7/87450.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 91,
    "turn_text": "Well, if the Democrats hold firm in the house, they can't block it. There's no filibuster in the house, and they can just put through the house pretty much what they want, unless there are defections from the blue dog Democrats. That's the danger. They have about a nine or 10 seat gap, which is very narrow, which means six blue dogs can turn the tide, and they will always be telling Speaker Pelosi, don't do this, don't do that, because we may not support you, and we may lose the next election in our conservative district. So there's an answer to all that. And that is to have a real progressive people-oriented agenda where you don't have to worry about blue dog Democrats because you'll have far more seats separating yourself as Democratic Party from the Republicans. But the Democrats haven't learned that lesson yet, that single payer for everybody, very",
