    "turn_text": "Well, thank you, Pam. She's referring to my book called Animal Envy, which is a fable. But the technique of a fable allowed a huge amount of experience in terms of what we know when we destroy animals and animal habitats around the planet, in terms of boomeranging against us. And of course, zuotic diseases, diseases transmitted to humans from animals have taken hundreds of millions of lives over modern history. I'm just think of malaria, for example. And it is important to be able to write about it in a way that youngsters can read about it and be educated, but be entertained in a constructive way. And that's what I tried to do with the book Animal Envy, which is still available by Seven Stories Press. It's not that long. And I would have hoped that some teachers would have adopted it as reading in school classes, but I don't think that's happening. Thank you for bringing this book to the attention of our listeners, Pam.",
