    "turn_idx": 175,
    "turn_text": "like to have Richard Trump go on the program. In fact, thank you for reminding us. He hasn't been the easiest person to get. He is sensitive to some of our criticisms of his directorship of the FLCIO. They have been nowhere near as aggressive. He has to deal with the public employee unions, which are very pro-corporate Democrat in philosophy, and the industrial unions, which would be more liberal, have been losing members in droves, and I understand he has that problem. He was not strong enough to push Obama for minimum wage increase or Obama promise. And when was the last time you saw a mass labor rally around the White House of the Congress? So he doesn't get out in the streets in terms of peaceful rallies. And he worked in the coal mines. He came up the ranks. He became a lawyer and was high in the United Mine Workers and then became AFL. So he had a resume that was very promising. The bureaucracy does things to people.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_03",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
    "explicit_propositions": [
